SUMMARY:2026 Lancaster Ride of Silence 
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRide leader: Carl Feldman
 \nSweep: Volunteer to Sweep\nAnticipated Average Pace: \\~10mph\nRoute: ht
 tps://ridewithgps.com/routes/54658728\n\nWe wont be silent about traffic v
 iolence but this will be a reflective bike ride through Lancaster in honor
  of cyclists who have been injured or killed on the roads. At 6pm we will 
 be joined by State Representatives Nikki Rivera and Smith Wade El as well 
 as representatives of the City of Lancaster and we will roll out at 6:30pm
 . Other officials pending.\n\n***Lancaster Ride of Silence 2026***\n\nJoin
  us for the **Ride of Silence.** This event is a powerful tribute to cycli
 sts and other vulnerable road users who have been injured or killed by dri
 vers on public roads. We don't need to be silent but it will be a ride to 
 raise awareness about sharing the road and honoring those we've lost. Let'
 s come together to show our support and solidarity for everyone that uses 
 the road outside of the protection of a car.\nThis is a no-drop\, group ri
 de. We'll meet at Ewell Plaza for a brief discussion then roll our way to 
 Noel Dorwart Park -- because road safety is for everyone is not only a cit
 y issue. The ride is approximately 10 miles with light hills in traffic\; 
 check out a [detailed ride map](https://ridewithgps.com/routes/54658728 "h
 ttps://ridewithgps.com/routes/54658728").\nHelmets are required. Remember 
 to bring lights\, too. Please wear a black and /or red ribbon in solidarit
 y for those who have been lost or injured. (easily made from a piece of cl
 oth or sock ). We may have some to pass out.\n\nCan you help make ribbons\
 , ghost bikes\, or ride marshall? Email Carl.Feldman@protonmail.com if you
  wish to assist.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3147091
 44/
